# Header

A header identifies the service and gives consistent access to its main destinations.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use a minimal identity header for a focused journey and add only the navigation, search or account information that users need. Keep the service name visible.

## When not to use it

Do not reproduce NHS branding or add a second application header inside Home Assistant views. A theme companion adapts supported native shell elements; it does not replace routing or authentication.

## Home Assistant adaptation

The NHS header’s identity rules apply to NHS services, not this project. civica.uk uses the supplied lockup and palette masthead. Preserve Home Assistant’s native menu, account actions and permissions. A constrained task may need fewer exits than a browsing dashboard.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a header landmark, an appropriately named home link and labelled navigation. Keep text and icons visible on every masthead colour, including yellow focus. Expose current navigation state without relying solely on an underline or colour.

